  "stories": 2,
  "description_text": "A rare opportunity to own a piece of Seattle history. Built in 1915 and designed by Bebb & Gould, this beautifully preserved Colonial Georgian home is a historically contributing home, with original masonry and old-world architectural details throughout. A grand entry staircase, illuminated by a skylight, welcomes you home. The east-facing living room opens directly onto the front patio, creating a lovely connection between indoor and outdoor living. It is an extraordinary setting for morning coffee, outdoor entertaining or simply enjoying the beauty of Montlake. An impressive chef's kitchen adjoins an intimate family room, perfect for reading, relaxing or building a personal library. The basement offers exceptional additional space for entertaining or creative pursuits. The location is truly extraordinary. Directly across the street, Seattle's newest park connects you to the Arboretum trails, pedestrian islands, the Ship Canal Waterfront Trail and Union Bay viewpoints. Enjoy kayaking, paddleboarding, cycling and the beauty of Lake Washington, just steps away. 8 minute walk to UW light rail station, convenient SR-520 access, bike lanes, the UW campus and Husky Stadium are all close by. Crew and game-day excitement are within earshot!",
