  "description_text": "A beautifully restored 1927 Tudor behind the gates of Seattle's coveted Broadmoor community, where tree-lined streets and distinctive homes surround the fairways of Broadmoor Golf Club. Classic brickwork, steep gables and a welcoming entry introduce interiors rich in architectural detail. Graceful archways, leaded-glass windows and a sweeping staircase pair with meticulously refinished hardwoods and freshly painted interiors. The light-filled living room features a Rumford fireplace and French doors to a covered garden terrace. An elegant formal dining room complements the kitchen's marble counters, premium range, herringbone porcelain floors and inviting breakfast nook. Upstairs, the primary suite offers a wood-burning fireplace, generous custom walk-in closet and bath with a freestanding soaking tub. Four bedrooms and a finished lower level provide room for guests, work and recreation. Mature landscaping frames a private backyard with level lawn and patios. A/C, heated floors and a detached two-car garage with EV charging complete the home. A peaceful retreat just minutes from Madison Park's cafes, boutiques and Lake Washington shoreline, as well as the trails of the Washington Park Arboretum.",
